  # MepS: OM DD-endopeptidase (Spr) after LpoA PBP1A activation.
  # MepS/Spr is the outer-membrane DD-endopeptidase that cleaves peptide
  # cross-links in existing sidewall PG so new strands polymerized by the
  # LpoA-stimulated PBP1A elongasome can insert without stress fracture.
  # Without MepS cleavage burn, LpoA-activated PG synthesis packs against
  # uncleaved sacculus and rod expansion stalls despite activator presence.
  # Domain: post-LpoA MepS/Spr OM DD-endopeptidase (not LpoA activator itself,
  # not PBP1A catalysis, not MepM/MepH redundant endopeptidases, not Slt lytic
  # TG, not LpoB/PBP1B septal path, not NlpD amidase activator, not scission).
  # Continuum: ...->roda->mreb->mrec->mred->rodz->pbp2->pbp1a->lpoa->meps
  #   (LpoA OM lipoprotein activator -> MepS/Spr OM DD-endopeptidase).
  # Pay take=min(n,atp,energy) - ATP stand-in for MepS cross-link cleavage cycle.
